File: src/server/checkout-route.ts. The supplied helper performs one commit. Signature: checkoutAtomic({ idempotencyKey, merchantId, basketId, items }) returns { outcome: created, orderId } or { outcome: replayed, orderId }. One commit claims the unique idempotency key, checks stock, decrements stock, writes the order and stores the replay response. Same key with same payload returns the stored orderId as replayed. Same key with a different payload throws KeyConflictError. Insufficient stock throws InsufficientStockError and rolls back. The current route is defective: it never reads idempotencyKey, it writes the order and decrements stock in two separate steps, and it always returns 201.
```ts
app.post('/api/checkout', async (req, res) => {
  const { merchantId, basketId, items } = req.body
  const order = await writeOrder(merchantId, basketId, items)
  await decrementStock(items)
  res.status(201).json({ orderId: order.id })
})
```
The route must read idempotencyKey, call the helper once, and map created to 201, replayed to 200, KeyConflictError to 409 and InsufficientStockError to 422.

