exemplar.en:
Decision. Session merchant M-104 owns C-9001, C-9003, C-9004 and C-9006, so four records are allowed. C-9002 belongs to M-207 and C-9005 to M-310. Both must return 404 with {"error":"not_found"} and no customer fields, because the contract uses the same response for non-owned and missing records to avoid revealing another merchant record. The supplied code leaks C-9002 by querying only customer_id and returning the full row. Patch the server query and response shape:
```ts
const row = await db.one<CustomerRow | null>(
  "SELECT customer_id, merchant_id, email, status FROM customers WHERE customer_id = $1 AND merchant_id = $2",
  [customerId, sessionMerchantId]
);
if (!row) return { status: 404, body: { error: "not_found" } };
return { status: 200, body: { customerId: row.customerId, email: row.email, status: row.status } };
```
Tests: owned C-9001 returns 200 with only customerId, email, status. Cross-tenant C-9002 returns 404 and no record fields. Missing C-9999 returns 404. Archived C-9003 returns 200 with status archived. Limitations: synthetic records only, no code executed, no claim about SHOPLINE production policy. Next: add server test and UI error state, then review with team lead.

