exemplar.en:
Decision: fund I1 atomic stock reservation. Evidence: fictional merchant-requests show 24 of 340 merchants report overselling after simultaneous online and in-store sales. Fictional inventory-incidents show 3,600 baseline monthly oversold orders and 62 sampled incidents traced to non-atomic reservation. These two sources agree on problem, impact and cause, so I1 passes Gate 1. I2 is medium evidence and ineligible. I3 is low evidence and costs HKD 185,000, above the HKD 150,000 hard budget. I1 costs HKD 96,000 and estimates 1,440 fewer oversold orders monthly. Remaining oversold orders: 3,600 minus 1,440 equals 2,160. Remaining budget: 150,000 minus 96,000 equals 54,000 HKD. Code correction:
```js
function reserveStock(db, sku, quantity) {
  const result = db.updateOne(
    { sku, available: { $gte: quantity } },
    { $inc: { available: -quantity } }
  );
  return result.modifiedCount === 1;
}
```
Uncertainty: survey response rate was 18 percent and the incident sample covered one week. Merchants are not identified. Next checks: instrument weekly oversold-order rate for affected SKUs against a control, and run a canary release before full rollout. Escalate to Ada Cheung if canary oversell rate does not fall by at least half the estimate.

exemplar.zh:
