exemplar.en:
Corrected code patch:

```ts
export function createOrder(
  idempotencyKey: string,
  payload: { amount: number, currency: string }
): { status: number, body: any } {
  if (!idempotencyKey || idempotencyKey.length > 64) {
    return { status: 400, body: { error: "invalid_idempotency_key" } }
  }
  if (orders.has(idempotencyKey)) {
    const existing = orders.get(idempotencyKey)!
    if (existing.amount === payload.amount && existing.currency === payload.currency) {
      return { status: 200, body: existing }
    }
    return { status: 409, body: { error: "idempotency_conflict" } }
  }
  const order = { id: `ord-${Date.now()}`, ...payload }
  orders.set(idempotencyKey, order)
  return { status: 201, body: order }
}
```

Why it fixes the defect: The original code does not validate the key length or presence, and it returns the existing order even when the payload differs. The corrected code checks key validity, compares payloads, and returns the correct status codes.

Proposed test cases and expected outcomes:
- Empty key: expect 400 invalid_idempotency_key.
- 65-character key: expect 400 invalid_idempotency_key.
- Retry with same key and same payload: expect 200 with original order.
- Retry with same key and different payload: expect 409 idempotency_conflict.
- New key: expect 201 with new order.

Limitations: No test for concurrent requests, no test for exactly 64-character key, and no real timeout simulation. These should be added.

Next steps: Add the above validation and payload comparison, then run the proposed tests in staging.

