Fictional app PulseDesk records each support request. Contract: input RequestPayload has fields userId, email, phone, message, ticketId, route, status, durationMs, errorCode. Output must be one log line. Current code logs the whole payload. Synthetic test observation: the log line includes email, phone, message and userId. No real customer data is used. Code is for reading only and must not be executed. The defect is logging personal fields without an allowlist.
```ts
type RequestPayload = {
  userId: string
  email: string
  phone: string
  message: string
  ticketId: string
  route: string
  status: number
  durationMs: number
  errorCode?: string
}

export function logRequest(payload: RequestPayload) {
  console.log(JSON.stringify({
    event: 'request_received',
    payload: payload
  }))
}
```

